{"id":"d7oc5dd8t45y9qv5lvc84k3kf","title":"维生素C或可预防消化过程中致癌化学物质的形成","originalTitle":"Vitamin C could help block cancer-linked chemicals in your stomach, study finds","summary":"研究人员通过数学模型发现，维生素C可能干扰消化过程中致癌化学物质的形成，尤其是在摄入含硝酸盐和亚硝酸盐的食物时。模型显示，餐后补充维生素C可适度降低这些化学物质的生成，但需进一步临床研究验证其对降低癌症风险的实际效果。","reason":null,"source":{"name":"ScienceDaily 综合"},"links":{"original":"https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/11/261114202236.htm"},"publishedAt":"2026-11-15T14:13:18.000Z","discoveredAt":"2026-11-16T16:59:52.836Z","timelineAt":"2026-11-16T16:59:52.836Z","category":"drug-therapy","tags":["研究成果","癌症免疫"],"score":47,"selected":false,"channel":"news","story":{"publicId":"3bb11a22-baef-4b15-97a1-8466ca05b688","title":"滑铁卢大学研究称维生素C或可降低硝酸盐相关致癌物生成"},"x":null,"readingMode":"full","author":null,"body":null,"outline":[],"relatedStories":[{"publicId":"3bb11a22-baef-4b15-97a1-8466ca05b688","title":"滑铁卢大学研究称维生素C或可降低硝酸盐相关致癌物生成"}],"topics":[{"slug":"cancer-immunotherapy","name":"癌症免疫治疗"}],"indexable":false,"markdownAvailable":true,"group":{"factId":"fg9O7dyE3KDM","reportCount":1,"additionalSourceCount":0},"hasTranslation":false,"bodyLanguage":"original"}